# Opinion

Meeting: 0023-continue-developing-the-software
Agent: Critic
Task: continue developing the software
Context:
- Shell parsing can be fragile; naive normalization could still emit malformed arrays or strip meaningful characters.
- Azure CLI flags must match App Service expectations; mis-typed healthCheckPath could silently fail without surfacing in CI.
Position:
- Guard against double-quoting or empty tokens when rebuilding scope arrays.
- Keep the default scope set intact even when users provide junk input so the UI stays usable.
Recommendations:
- Sanitize scopes by removing brackets/quotes, splitting on commas/whitespace, and rebuilding the array only when tokens remain; otherwise fall back to the default list.
- Validate that workflow snippets literally contain `healthCheckPath="/healthz"` and `/readyz` to align with documentation and tests.
- Consider escaping all interpolated strings to avoid breaking JSON when secrets contain quotes.
